Z||000000||ChadMan||07-03-2001||02:27 PM||||So I'm surfing eBay looking at old issues of Car and Driver for sale.  I had forgotten just how bad late 70's-early 80's cars sucked.  No wonder the Fiero was such a big hit!<P>Some sample articles:<P>4/79:  "Fire Arrow: Plymouth's pocket rocket takes us into the performance-car future"<P>7/79:  "Project Fairmont!" (I $hit you not.)<P>11/79: "Top Ten Fuelers: Colt, Rabbit Diesel, Dasher Diesel, Civic, Datsun 210, MB 240D, Subaru GL, Mazda GLC, Corolla, Chevette"<P>1/80:  "Skylark vs. Accord vs. Saab 900 vs. Audi 4000:  What happens when an X-car takes on the world's best sports sedans?"<P>5/80: "To Terilingua in two Fiats"<P>9/80: "Chrysler's new K-Car:  Did Uncle Sam get his money's worth?"<BR>(Note: This issue also shows "Spy Report: Pontiac's little two-seater comes to life!")<P>1/81: "Peugeot Turbodiesel: Efficiency Express"<P>2/81: "Le Project Car" (they try to make a sports car out of a Renault)<BR>(Note: This issue also shows "1983 P-car: Pontiac's sportscar prototype unveiled")<P>3/81: Two winners here.<BR>1)  "Ford EXP: Ford bets a bundle, hoping for another Mustang miracle"<BR>2)  "Olds Omega vs. Chevy Malibu: straightforward answers to complex questions"<P>6/81: Buick Regal vs. Toyota Supra comparison test.  (Next month: Apples vs. Oranges!)<P>7/81: "Pontiac Grand Prix Diesel: Yesterday's big shot bites the fuel-economy bullet"<P>Just when things looked like they'd never improve, 1982 brought better news:  the new Camaro/Firebird, the return of the 5.0 Mustang, the 944, and "We drive Pontiac's top-secret P-car" (6/82).<P>How did we ever sink so low as 1979-1981?||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||07-03-2001||04:06 PM||||Yeah, forget about the DeLorean when we can have (sarcastic whooping) the Camaro and Firebird... sheesh..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
